Blink: stopping a find, or starting a new one, cancels the pending scroll.

TextFinder::FindInternal() scrolls to the match it makes active in a task
for the next animation frame (scroll_task_), and TextFinder::Scroll() adds
the match's marker back, active, when no text-match marker covers it. Only
the next match found cancelled that task: neither StopFindingAndClearSelection()
nor a new session did. A stop (or a new search that finds nothing in the
frame) before the next frame removed every marker, and then the scroll put
the old active match back, painted orange, with nothing to clear it again
(Chrome's own find path, so its find bar would show it as well). Seen with
zebkit_view_stop_finding(CLEAR) after a search with no match, mostly on a
slow Windows machine, where no frame came between the searches and the
stop; on Linux by stopping right after a search. Both now cancel the
task (a forced redo of a session, which reuses the active match, keeps it).
Chromium 157's code and the scroll task's comment ("another Find ... would
have been canceled") show no upstream fix.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/editing/finder/text_finder.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/editing/finder/text_finder.cc
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/editing/finder/text_finder.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/editing/finder/text_finder.cc
@@ -177,6 +177,12 @@
 void TextFinder::InitNewSession(const mojom::blink::FindOptions& options) {
   should_locate_active_rect_ = false;
   CancelPendingScopingEffort();
+  // zebkit: the previous session's scroll to its active match, still waiting
+  // for an animation frame, would mark that match active again in a session
+  // that may have no match at all. A forced redo keeps it (FindInternal
+  // reuses the active match then).
+  if (!options.force)
+    scroll_task_.Cancel();
   if (!options.find_match) {
     // This gets called in FindInternal if a match is found, but FindInternal
     // doesn't run when find_match is false, so we need to do it here in case
@@ -463,6 +469,10 @@
 
 void TextFinder::StopFindingAndClearSelection() {
   CancelPendingScopingEffort();
+  // zebkit: a scroll to the active match still waiting for an animation
+  // frame would add its marker back, active, after every marker is removed
+  // below: a highlight that stays after the search has stopped.
+  scroll_task_.Cancel();
 
   // Remove all markers for matches found and turn off the highlighting.
   OwnerFrame().GetFrame()->GetDocument()->Markers().RemoveMarkersOfTypes(
